<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ershi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ershi was the capital of Dayuan, the kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergana-valley">Ferghana</a> valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> known to Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> for its 'heavenly horses'. In 102 BCE the Han general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-guangli">Li Guangli</a> besieged it and cut off its water supply until the nobles killed their king and agreed to hand over horses. Its exact location is uncertain.</p></div>
